\ Test that the restructured three-way polymorphic arithmetic path
\ (fixnum / float / native fallback) works correctly for all
\ fixnum and float combinations. The non-numeric fallback path is
\ structurally present but not triggered until non-numeric types
\ reach compiled arithmetic (e.g., after fixnum overflow fallback
\ in 222.2).

add:  ( a b -- c ) [ + ] ;
sub:  ( a b -- c ) [ - ] ;
mul:  ( a b -- c ) [ * ] ;
fdiv: ( a b -- c ) [ / ] ;
mod:  ( a b -- c ) [ % ] ;

\ === Fixnum + fixnum ===
3 4 add .
10 3 sub .
5 6 mul .
10 3 fdiv .
7 3 mod .

\ === Mixed fixnum + float ===
3 2.5 add .
2.5 3 add .
10 2.5 sub .
10.0 3 sub .
4 2.5 mul .
2.5 4 mul .
7 2.0 fdiv .
7.0 2 fdiv .
7 2.0 mod .
7.0 2 mod .

\ === Float + float ===
2.5 1.5 add .
4.5 1.5 sub .
2.5 1.5 mul .
7.5 2.5 fdiv .
7.5 2.0 mod .

\ === Edge cases ===
0 2.5 add .
3.0 0 mul .
-3 2.5 add .
4 -1.5 mul .
3.0 2 add .
2 3.0 sub .
